ations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that you should use "},{"code":"g_iconv()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for streaming conversions."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Despite the fact that ","type":"text"},{"code":"bytesRead","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can return information about partial"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"characters, the g_convert_… functions are not generally suitable"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"for streaming. If the underlying converter maintains internal state,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"then this won’t be preserved across successive calls to "},{"code":"g_convert()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_convert_with_iconv()"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"g_convert_with_fallback()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". (An example of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this is the GNU C converter for CP1255 which does not emit a base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"character until it knows that the next character is not a mark that"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"could combine with the base character.)"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Characters which are valid in the input character set, but which have no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation in the output character set will result in a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"illegalSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" error. This is in contrast to the "},{"code":"iconv()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specification, which leaves this behaviour implementation defined. Note that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"this is the same error code as is returned for an invalid byte sequence in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the input character set. To get defined behaviour for conversion of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unrepresentable characters, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_convert_with_fallback()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/convertWithIconv(str:len:converter:bytesRead:bytesWritten:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Function","externalID":"s:4GLib16convertWithIconv3str3len9converter9bytesRead0H7WrittenSSSgSPys4Int8VGSg_SiSpySo7_GIConvVGSpySuGSgAQtKF","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"title":"convertWithIconv(str:len:converter:bytesRead:bytesWritten:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"convertWithIconv","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"str","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnsafePointer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SP"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"text":"gchar","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">!, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"len","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"gssize","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gssize"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"converter"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GIConv","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@GIConv"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"bytesRead"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sp","text":"UnsafeMutablePointer"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gsize","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"gsize"},{"text":">!, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bytesWritten","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnsafeMutablePointer","kind":"typeIdentifier","